body:
Surfaces a `CopyEvent` whenever paintcannon issues a clipboard request. `success` indicates whether the request was issued successfully; whether the terminal accepts it and updates the system clipboard is technically dependent on the terminal.
### CopyEvent payload
```
  {
    type: "copy";
    text: string;
    success: boolean; // Whether the clipboard request was successfully issued
  }
  ```
  Clanker-updated README and copy-example demo.
  
<img width="2171" height="923" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/895f2542-4b95-4473-8ff2-0ecd23ecf5d4" />

  
  \* \- **Known issue:** in iTerm2 for Mac, a mouse-release off-terminal will not result in a clipboard event. Seeing that this is the case in `opencode` as well, marking it as out of scope for this PR.
